<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KFA buys 157,500 tonnes of corn.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KFA buys 157,500 tonnes of corn.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Feed Association's (KFA) office in Pusan bought 52,500 tonnes of corn from Cargill on Monday and 105,000 tonnes from Toepfer on late Wednesday, an official with KFA said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The official said arrival was slated for Pusan and Ulsan.</p>
<p>The sellers have the option for shipment and prices are varied.</p>
<p>Details for the purchases are as follows:</p>
<p> DATE  TONNE  SELLER  PRICE   SHIPMENT		     ETA</p>
<p> 20   52,500 Cargill $140.90 Mar 1-20 (PNW)	     Mar 30</p>
<p>				&quot;    Feb 9-28 (Gulf)	    Mar 30</p>
<p>			   $140.10 Mar 11-30 (China)	  Mar 30</p>
<p> 22   52,500 Toepfer $137.20 Mar 20-Apr 8 (PNW)	 Apr 20</p>
<p>				&quot;    Mar 1-20 (Gulf)	    Apr 20</p>
<p>				&quot;    Mar 1-20 (Argentina)     Apr 20</p>
<p> 22   52,500 Toepfer $134    Apr 10-29 (PNW)	    May 10</p>
<p>				&quot;    Mar 22-Apr 10 (Gulf)     May 10</p>
<p>				&quot;    Mar 20-Apr 8 (Argentina) May 10</p>
<p>			   $129    Apr 21- May 10 (China)   May 10</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
